      "role": "user",
      "content": "the plan stopped cut off at the end but that looks fine so far. one thing though, i'm worried about getting too tired or hitting a wall halfway through the month. how should i handle it if the weights start feeling way too heavy or if i feel like i'm running out of gas during a set?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's important to listen to your body, especially as you're starting a new workout routine. If your weights start feeling too heavy:\n1. Pause and reassess your form - doing the exercise correctly is more important than going through the motions without proper form.\n2. Cut back on weight or reps - considering your goal's progression, slightly lower the weights while maintaining proper form.\n3. Rest or switch exercises - Take an extra rest day if needed to recover.\n\nIf you find you're consistently struggling with high-energy expenditure or hitting a plateau, it might be beneficial to include a couple of full rest days throughout the week, or even replace a session with a lighter or lower-intensity workout focused on recovery. Remember, consistent workouts with appropriate recovery are key to building strength over time, not just sheer gym time. Also, consider varying your workouts to avoid plateaus and keep mentally engaged.",
